    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="eef20ef3-3b1b-5eb8-93e7-dbdcc79728ba" activityNameId="dc6c7634-7b82-5425-984f-5d29c709a958" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Heat, residential, by combustion of synthetic natural gas from catalytic methanation using boiler, distribu [224e874cbd]</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Heat, residential, by combustion of synthetic natural gas from catalytic methanation using boiler, distributed by pipeline, produced by Electrolysis, PEM using electricity from grid and carbon sourced from MSWI (100:0 alloc.)
This dataset represents the supply of 1 megajoule of heat in a residence, by synthetic natural gas from catalytic methanation combustion in a boiler.  The synthetic natural gas from catalytic methanation is produced by  Electrolysis, PEM, with electricity from grid as feedstock. The carbon is sourced from MSWI. Heat conversion efficiency [% LHV input]: 109.5%. LHV [MJ/kg]: 48. Market price [Euro/MJ]: 0.03. Distribution loss [% output]: 0.02%. Storage loss [% output]: 0%. CO2 biogenic share [%]: 52%. Power [kW]: 16.4. Lifetime [years]: 20. Annual operation [hours]: 2100. : .  For more information, refer to: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023. Source: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023.

 UUID: 0abeca47-6be9-3454-9adf-60e2da2e6eae
Location: 
Technology: 
Time period: 
Production volume: 
Sampling: Sampling procedure: Literature data
